# Caching & Media (ADR-007, ADR-008, ADR-009)

## Never Cache (page cache or CDN)

Cart, checkout, my-account, order confirmation / thank-you, QR / redemption
endpoints, payment callbacks and webhooks, wp-admin, and ANY logged-in
response. Serving one visitor's cart or account to another is a
critical-severity bug.

## Object Cache (Redis — planned infrastructure)

- Every key includes the site ID: `bc:{blog_id}:...`.
- Redis is NEVER the source of truth — every cached value must be rebuildable
  from the database.
- Platform requires `WP_REDIS_SELECTIVE_FLUSH` + distinct `WP_REDIS_PREFIX`
  per site. NEVER flush the whole network's cache for one hall's change.
- Code must not assume Redis exists (it is planned infrastructure): always
  use the WordPress object-cache API (`wp_cache_get/set/delete` with cache
  groups), never call Redis clients directly.

## Page Cache & CDN (planned infrastructure)

- Public catalog pages may be page-cached; cache MUST vary by Host so each
  hall subdomain is its own namespace.
- Content mutations (product save, price/stock change, session/availability
  change) trigger a TARGETED purge of affected URLs only (product page,
  category/tag archives, shop page) through one central helper. Never
  "purge everything" on a content edit.
- Goal (D-005): hall manager edits → normal browser refresh shows it.
  HTML: `Cache-Control: no-cache`. Static assets: long TTL + versioned URLs.

## Media

- Product images offload to S3-compatible storage via a plugin with CONFIRMED
  Multisite support (per-site paths like `sites/{blog_id}/`). Vendor is open
  (S3 / R2 / Spaces) — never hardcode vendor SDKs (ADR-009).
- Local disk is acceptable ONLY in local dev; production never stores uploads
  on local disk long-term.
- Validate uploads (MIME, extension, dimensions, size). No unrestricted SVG
  uploads by hall users. Serve AVIF with WebP fallback via CDN.
